#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:30
msgid ""
"Supports UB, L1, L0A, L0B, L0C and SS in the Ascend scheduled pipeline. Each "
"placed storage must also have an explicit positive version count "
"in :func:`annotate_buffer_versions`, including ``1`` for unversioned "
"storage. A mode without a count, inferred versions, and manual multi-buffer "
"metadata alone do not satisfy this requirement. Annotation order does not "
"matter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:36
msgid ""
"Addresses are non-negative Python integers, aligned to 32 bytes for UB/SS, "
"512 for L1/L0A/L0B, and 1024 for L0C. A placement includes all physical "
"versions and layout padding; views of one storage share the same base. Bound "
"L0 scale-factor handles follow their data buffer's placement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:41
msgid ""
"Partial maps are allowed. Other allocations in a placed pool use the first "
"aligned free interval, without storage reuse. Overlap is rejected even for "
"disjoint lifetimes or positive conflict hints. Different pools and private "
"AIV UBs have independent addresses; common UB storage reserves both UBs. "
"Placement does not change synchronization or ownership."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:47
msgid ""
"Every allocation in a placed pool must have a positive static physical size "
"and fit its hardware capacity, including the 32 KiB UB reservation for SIMT. "
"Pools without placements retain their ordinary allocation behavior."
msgstr ""

