#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:61
msgid ""
"When using T.Persistent with num_stages > 1, the Z3 auto-scheduler computes "
"optimal buffer version counts for each on-chip buffer. Each mapping value "
"may be one of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:65
msgid ""
"``1``: opt out of multi-buffer eligibility, including explicit owner claims;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:66
msgid "``num_versions >= 2``: use a fixed version count and automatic mode;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:67
msgid "``(num_versions, mode)``: use a fixed count and explicit mode;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:68
msgid ""
"``mode``: select a mode while leaving the version count to the scheduler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:70
msgid ""
"``mode`` is ``\"auto\"``, ``\"iteration\"``, or ``\"counter\"``. "
"``\"iteration\"`` uses the affine flattened-loop index. ``\"counter\"`` uses "
"a monotonic local counter that advances after a completed active buffer "
"epoch. ``\"auto\"`` keeps the affine fast path when safe and selects a "
"counter for conditionally executed or non-affine epochs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:76
msgid ""
"A fixed count is useful when you want to guarantee double-buffering for a "
"critical buffer regardless of the Z3 solver's choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:79
msgid ""
"``{buf: 1}`` removes the storage (including aliases) from multi-buffer "
"eligibility, overriding inferred or explicit owner claims and preserving "
"ordinary dependencies instead of owner-exclusion dependencies. Overriding "
"explicit ``multi_buffer_eligible`` claims emits a warning once per storage. "
"Use this when the eligibility heuristic misses reads of previous data. To "
"keep eligibility with one version, explicitly specify a mode: ``{buf: (1, "
"\"auto\")}``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:86
msgid ""
"AutoSchedule consumes this map and replaces it with the selected version "
"counts, including versions chosen automatically by the solver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:110
msgid ""
"Unlike :func:`annotate_buffer_versions` (which asks the Z3 auto-scheduler to "
"version a buffer for you), this annotation tells AutoSchedule that the "
"buffer is *already* multi-buffered by hand: the user writes the version "
"index into every access themselves (e.g. ``buf[l % 2]`` / ``buf[(l + 1) % "
"2]`` ping-pong), and the pass only needs to analyze dependencies and emit "
"the ``set_flag`` / ``wait_flag`` synchronization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:117
msgid ""
"The per-buffer version count ``N`` is used as the ring size / the upper "
"bound on the cross-iteration distance the analysis searches for — it does "
"NOT reshape or reallocate the buffer and does NOT assume the version index "
"lives in dimension 0. Each positional argument is either:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:122
msgid ""
"a bare buffer: ``N`` defaults to its leading dimension ``buffer.shape[0]`` "
"(which must then be a compile-time constant) — the common "
"``T.alloc_shared((N, ...))`` ping-pong case; or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:125
msgid ""
"a ``{buffer: N}`` dict: gives ``N`` explicitly, decoupled from the shape. "
"Use this when the buffer has no dedicated leading version dim — e.g. a "
"flattened buffer multi-buffered by disjoint sub-ranges — or when you want a "
"version count that differs from ``shape[0]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:146
msgid ""
"When unlimit'd, a scope's capacity is effectively unbounded so Z3 will not "
"constrain multi-buffer versions based on that memory pool. Use this when you "
"know a particular scope has spare headroom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/annotations/index.rst:150
msgid ""
"Valid scopes: ``\"shared\"``, ``\"shared.l1\"``, ``\"shared.l0c\"``, "
"``\"shared.l0a\"``, ``\"shared.l0b\"``."
msgstr ""
